WEBVTT

00:00:04.364 --> 00:00:05.614
What's that?

00:00:06.199 --> 00:00:09.910
An address of a very old
acquaintance of mine.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.373
A safe house in Paris
reinforced with enchantments.

00:00:14.541 --> 00:00:16.625
Safe house?
Why would I need a safe house in Paris?

00:00:16.793 --> 00:00:20.296
One hopes you won't, but should things
at some point go terribly wrong,

00:00:20.463 --> 00:00:21.880
it's good to have a place to go.

00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:24.633
You know, for a cup of tea.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.176
No. No, no, no.

00:00:26.261 --> 00:00:27.428
- (ENGINE STARTING)
- Absolutely not.

00:00:27.971 --> 00:00:30.222
No, 'cause I'm banned from
international travel, Dumbledore.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.807
If I leave the country,
they will put me in Azkaban,

00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:33.309
and they will throw away the key.

00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:35.769
- Do you know why I admire you, Newt?
- What?

00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:39.023
More, perhaps, than any man I know.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.193
You do not seek power.

00:00:44.029 --> 00:00:45.237
Or popularity.

00:00:45.947 --> 00:00:50.617
You simply ask,
is a thing right in itself?

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:54.413
If it is, you do it no matter the cost.

00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:57.207
That's all very well, Dumbledore,
but forgive me for asking.

00:00:57.375 --> 00:00:59.084
Why can't you go?

00:01:04.966 --> 00:01:06.967
I cannot move against Grindelwald.

00:01:10.513 --> 00:01:11.930
It has to be you.

00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:20.105
Well, I can't blame you.

00:01:20.273 --> 00:01:22.858
In your shoes, I'd probably refuse too.

00:01:23.026 --> 00:01:25.402
- What?
- It's late. Good evening, Newt.

00:01:25.487 --> 00:01:26.695
Wait, no.

00:01:27.781 --> 00:01:29.114
Oh, come on.

00:01:30.492 --> 00:01:32.076
- (AIR WHOOSHES)
- (NEWT SCOFFS)

00:01:39.876 --> 00:01:41.085
(PICKETT SQUEAKING)

00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:44.880
(SIGHS) Dumbledore.

00:01:59.562 --> 00:02:00.896
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:02:18.081 --> 00:02:19.540
(SQUEAKING)

00:02:30.385 --> 00:02:31.510
(SQUEALS)

00:02:31.636 --> 00:02:32.761
(POT CLATTERS)

00:02:32.846 --> 00:02:34.138
(SQUEAKING)

00:02:34.973 --> 00:02:36.807
(BABY NIFFLER GRUNTING)

00:02:44.357 --> 00:02:45.774
(SQUEALING)

00:02:50.196 --> 00:02:51.196
Bunty!

00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:54.867
Bunty!

00:02:58.163 --> 00:03:01.373
Bunty, the baby Nifflers
are loose again.

00:03:01.499 --> 00:03:03.125
(CREATURE BRAYING)

00:03:13.303 --> 00:03:14.511
NEWT: Well done.

00:03:14.721 --> 00:03:16.054
I'm so sorry, Newt.
They must've picked the lock

00:03:16.222 --> 00:03:18.223
- while I was cleaning out the Augureys.
- Not to worry.

00:03:18.683 --> 00:03:19.683
BUNTY: Hmm.

00:03:25.231 --> 00:03:26.732
I fed nearly everyone.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.192
Pinky's had his nose drops and...

00:03:28.401 --> 00:03:29.401
And Elsie?

00:03:29.486 --> 00:03:30.944
Elsie's droppings
are nearly normal again.

00:03:31.112 --> 00:03:32.112
Wonderful.

00:03:33.198 --> 00:03:35.908
You can, um... You can clock off now.

00:03:38.828 --> 00:03:41.622
- I told you to leave the kelpie to me.
- That wound needs more ointment.

00:03:41.706 --> 00:03:43.123
I don't want you losing fingers over it.

00:03:53.259 --> 00:03:55.969
Seriously, you go home now, Bunty.

00:03:57.347 --> 00:03:58.555
You must be exhausted.

00:03:58.723 --> 00:04:00.432
You know the kelpie's easier with two.

00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:02.434
(KELPIE CALLING)

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.523
Perhaps you should take off your shirt.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.235
Don't worry.

00:04:11.694 --> 00:04:13.237
I'll dry off quick enough.

00:04:13.613 --> 00:04:14.613
(BUNTY INHALES SHARPLY)

00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:27.834
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:04:35.218 --> 00:04:36.635
(GASPING)

00:04:46.354 --> 00:04:47.521
(NEWT WHOOPING)

00:04:50.191 --> 00:04:51.441
(GRUNTING)

00:04:54.821 --> 00:04:56.905
Someone needed to let off some steam.

00:04:57.156 --> 00:04:58.490
Ointment, Bunty.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.080
(KELPIE GROWLS)

00:05:05.164 --> 00:05:07.833
You bite Bunty again,
and there'll be trouble, mister.

00:05:08.376 --> 00:05:09.668
(GLASS SHATTERING)

00:05:11.004 --> 00:05:12.129
What was that?

00:05:12.672 --> 00:05:13.922
I don't know.

00:05:16.301 --> 00:05:18.093
But I want you to go home now, Bunty.

00:05:18.261 --> 00:05:19.636
- Shall I call the Ministry?
- No.

00:05:19.804 --> 00:05:21.555
I want you to go home. Please.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.477
(WAND TINKLING)

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.316
WOMAN: Just give me the pieces.
MAN: I got it.

00:05:32.483 --> 00:05:34.026
WOMAN: Honey, if you could just
give it to me...

00:05:34.193 --> 00:05:35.652
MAN: He doesn't care.

00:05:35.737 --> 00:05:37.738
If you could just give this
to me, sweetheart.

00:05:43.036 --> 00:05:45.037
- (VASE SMASHES)
- Hey!

00:05:45.788 --> 00:05:48.915
Newt! Get over here, you maniac.

00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:51.293
- (JACOB LAUGHING)
- We hope you don't mind, Newt.

00:05:51.461 --> 00:05:52.461
We let ourselves in.

00:05:52.545 --> 00:05:55.088
It's rainin' out there, cats and dogs.

00:05:55.465 --> 00:05:56.673
London's cold.

00:05:56.841 --> 00:05:58.342
You were supposed
to have been obliviated.

00:05:58.509 --> 00:06:00.052
(LAUGHING) I know.

00:06:00.219 --> 00:06:01.678
It didn't work, pal.

00:06:02.055 --> 00:06:03.055
I mean, you said it.

00:06:03.222 --> 00:06:05.182
The potion only erases bad memories.

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:06.350
I didn't have any.

00:06:06.517 --> 00:06:08.685
I mean, uh, don't get me wrong.
I had some weird ones,

00:06:08.853 --> 00:06:10.437
and I had some scary ones.

00:06:10.688 --> 00:06:11.772
But this angel...

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:16.652
This angel over here,
she filled me in on all the bad parts,

00:06:16.736 --> 00:06:18.820
and, uh, here we are, I guess, huh?

00:06:18.988 --> 00:06:21.448
- (ALL LAUGH)
- This is wonderful.

00:06:23.785 --> 00:06:25.369
- (JACOB MOANS)
- NEWT: Wait. Is...

00:06:26.871 --> 00:06:29.623
Tina? Tina?

00:06:30.708 --> 00:06:31.792
(JACOB SIGHS)

00:06:31.876 --> 00:06:33.877
Oh, it's just us, honey.

00:06:35.088 --> 00:06:36.588
Me and Jacob.

00:06:36.881 --> 00:06:38.173
Oh.

00:06:38.257 --> 00:06:39.841
QUEENIE: Why don't I
make us some dinner, huh?

00:06:40.009 --> 00:06:41.176
JACOB: Yes!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.803
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:06:46.057 --> 00:06:47.265
Hey, honey.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:48.850
Teen and I aren't talking.

00:06:49.936 --> 00:06:52.979
- NEWT: Why?
- Oh, well, you know...

00:06:53.147 --> 00:06:54.564
She found out about
Jacob and I seeing each other,

00:06:54.732 --> 00:06:57.484
and she didn't like it,
'cause of the law.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.236
Not allowed to... Oop!

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.238
Not allowed to date No-Majs,

00:07:01.698 --> 00:07:04.074
not allowed to marry them.
Blah, blah, blah.

00:07:05.201 --> 00:07:08.745
Well, she was all in a tizzy anyway
'cause of you.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.623
- Me?
- Yeah, you, Newt.

00:07:11.791 --> 00:07:13.500
It was in Spellbound.

00:07:13.918 --> 00:07:16.086
Here. I brought it for you.

